//! A JavaScript application on a UI tree, with the SilkJS engine embedded in the process.
//!
//! JavaScript runs on the thread that owns the tree. It builds nodes through native functions
//! that append to one ui-protocol batch, and it receives each event between the tree's `begin`
//! and `finish`, so `preventDefault()` in a handler decides that event's default action. Start
//! at [`JsHost`].
pub import host { JsHost, JsError }
pub import bridge { Bridge, LogEntry }
